# RDF 3.9.4 Release Notes

## 3.9.4

-- New Features --

[New] rdf-claims agent (opus · high): fresh-context claims check of text before it is posted (PR bodies,
      commit and squash messages, changelogs, issue and chat drafts); pins the state and hashes the text,
      derives each answer from the primary record before comparing, and gives closed-set verdicts with
      replacements; Edit is disallowed and its prompt limits writes to a report, evidence and scratch
[New] rdf tokens: with no tool option the report covers Claude Code and, when the scope has Codex usage, Codex
      too (combined spend line, one section per tool, top five sessions by cost); --claude and --codex report
      one tool; the default --json and --summary carry source "all", the combined cost_usd and a claude and a codex
      object (null when that tool has no data)
[New] rdf tokens --all: every project, each project dir read once by its physical path, with a by-project table;
      a Codex rollout counts toward its deepest ancestor that is a Claude Code project cwd or whose slug names a
      project dir (aliases resolve to the physical dir), else the project whose slug its path names, else its cwd
[New] rdf tokens --by day|week|month|session|project: one table instead of the full report (day, week and month in
      local time; project implies --all); --top N sets the rows in the session and by-project tables
[New] rdf tokens row cache (~/.rdf/cache/tokens, RDF_TOKENS_CACHE, --no-cache): rows are extracted once per
      transcript or rollout and re-extracted when its mtime (or its subagent meta's) differs from the entry's;
      entries hold usage metadata and Codex quota samples, never message content, mode 0600, under a root named
      by a checksum of the extraction program (roots unused for more than a week are pruned)
[New] rdf run claude|codex [@account] [-y|--yolo | --root | --sandbox]: launch Claude Code or Codex for an
      account (rdf c and rdf x for short); --yolo is --dangerously-skip-permissions (claude) or
      --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox (codex); --root (claude) adds IS_SANDBOX=1 so --yolo runs as root
      and isolates nothing; --sandbox runs the tool's own sandbox with permission checks kept (claude: strict
      sandbox settings plus acceptEdits; codex: workspace-write, on-request) and refuses flags that undo it;
      claude also takes --chrome and --fs; the account comes from @name, rdf use (RDF_ACCOUNT),
      RDF_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT or rdf account default, a stale name fails closed, and a codex account pick drops
      CODEX_API_KEY and CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN
[New] rdf review: codex exec for an account with a read-only sandbox (--write for workspace-write), --effort, -m,
      -o and -C; a text prompt goes after -- with stdin closed, and -f FILE or - passes the prompt on stdin
[New] rdf shell init: an rdf shell function whose rdf use sets the account for rdf run and rdf review in this
      shell (every other command passes through to the binary), and bash/zsh tab completion for rdf subcommands,
      options, @accounts and account names (zsh through bashcompinit when compinit is loaded)
[New] rdf account: Codex homes, ~/.codex-<name>, for non-primary accounts when ~/.codex exists (add creates one,
      link adds missing ones), linking whichever of config.toml, AGENTS.md, history.jsonl, prompts, rules, skills,
      sessions and archived_sessions exist in ~/.codex (sessions and archived_sessions are created there first)
      while auth.json and state stay per home; list shows a CODEX column and dir --codex prints the home

-- Changes --

[Change] agent counts 6 -> 7 in README, RDF.md, WORKFORCE.md and docs/index.md; WORKFORCE lists rdf-claims
         in the org chart, model summary and agent details
[Change] tests: seven behavioral contracts for the claims checker; live agent-meta emission covers
         claims.md tools and disallowedTools; the 3.6.5 fixture test compares frontmatter for every agent in
         the frozen tar and pins the tar's agent list to the frozen 3.7.0 catalog
[Change] rdf tokens (Codex): a project's scope also covers rollouts run from its Claude Code scratchpads (a path
         component equal to the project's slug), which some Claude-launched codex exec runs use as their cwd
[Change] rdf tokens: extraction runs in parallel workers (RDF_TOKENS_JOBS, default the CPU count) that grep-filter
         each file and run one jq per batch of files; one message's consecutive entries with the same metadata cache
         as one row; a window run reads each Codex rollout once instead of up to three times
[Change] rdf tokens: the default transcript root follows CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR; Codex archived_sessions rollouts are
         read; --session falls back to a Codex thread when no Claude Code transcript has the id (an id neither
         tool has still exits 1); --transcripts implies --claude; --since is documented as UTC midnight
[Change] rdf shell init no longer defines claude, c, cs, ch or cuse: use rdf c, rdf c -y (rdf c --root where
         init had --sandbox, which was IS_SANDBOX=1 plus skipped permissions, not a sandbox), rdf c --chrome and
         rdf use; init --sandbox now only prints that hint, so 3.9 eval lines keep working
[Change] rdf help, README and quickstart describe rdf run, rdf c, rdf x, rdf review and rdf use, and docs/index
         rdf run and rdf use; the README rdf help block is re-synced with rdf help; rdf account hints point at
         rdf run
[Change] tests: run.bats (new) covers rdf run, rdf c/x, rdf review, credential drop and @mention pass-through;
         shell.bats covers the rdf function, rdf use and bash and zsh completion, including a real-terminal check
         that @account completion keeps the @; account.bats covers Codex homes

-- Bug Fixes --

[Fix] rdf tokens (Codex): record lines are read as text (grep -a, C locale), so a rollout with a NUL byte or
      invalid UTF-8 can no longer lose the rows grep would have suppressed as binary
